Launch a workflow script: plain JavaScript in an isolated VM. The call returns a background workflow id immediately; the script's return value is its consolidated JSON result. title (a few words) names the run's row. Use subagent for one bounded task and parallel subagent launches for flat independent work; use a workflow for scripted dependencies, pipelines or structured aggregation. Ultracode is on when the <workflow> system-prompt section says so or the user's latest prompt says ultracode. Launch is refused while it is off; management still works.

Manage with {action: "status", id?} to list runs or inspect one, {action: "result", id} to retrieve its outcome, or {action: "stop", id} to stop it. Only one workflow may be active at a time.

The script reaches only:
- agent(prompt, { agentType, tier?, schema?, label?, phase? }): launches one child and resolves to its final text, or with schema (a JSON Schema object) to the validated value; it rejects when the child fails. agentType is an agent from the subagent tool's list. tier runs that agent on another pin: one of {{ $tiers | join ", " }}; frontier is refused, and the default is the agent's own tier. label (a few words) titles its row. phase (a few words) lists it under that phase, overriding phase(). model, effort and isolation are refused.
- phase(title): later agent() calls default to this phase, as a stage heading.
- parallel([() => agent(...), ...]): runs the thunks concurrently; results in order, null where one failed.
- pipeline(items, ...stages): each item runs through stage(previous, item, index) on its own, with no barrier between stages; null where a stage failed.
- log(message): adds a line to the result, as console.log does.
- args: the call's args value.
A leading `export const meta = {...}` is ignored. Nothing else is reachable: no files, shell, network, timers or modules.

Notes:
{{- with get $sizes .workflow_size }}
- Keep a run under {{ . }} agents.
{{- end }}
- Plan mode admits read-only agents only.
- One writer per write scope: broker approval is not write isolation, so give concurrent writers disjoint files.
- The run shows as one fleet row; Enter on it lists its agents by phase. Root steering does not rewrite the running script; steer named children through existing subagent controls. Root Escape or Ctrl+Enter interrupts the root response, not the workflow; use stop to cancel the workflow.
